  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Tamkeen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Mauritania):  .Through the USAID Tamkeen activity, the U.S. government will.continue supporting civil society and non-governmental organizations to work.with vulnerable Mauritanian youth and build social cohesion through positive.approaches for civic engagement and alternatives to violent extremism (VE)..USAID Tamkeen will build on the progress attained through previous youth.activities to address the vestiges of Mauritania&apos;s historic slavery system, the.continuation of discrimination of minority groups, and the large, unemployed.youth population. USAID Tamkeen will also strive to reduce pull factors that.drive youth and others to join violent extremist organizations (VEOs). USAID.Tamkeen invests in youth and women as change agents to engage in activism to.combat the spread of mis/disinformation. At-risk Mauritanians, particularly.youth, underrepresented ethnic groups, and women, are vulnerable to recruitment.by VEOs. This vulnerability to recruitment has been further exacerbated by.social distancing measures required to stop the spread of the COVID-19 pandemic.and the subsequent economic downturn. USAID Tamkeen aims to create mutual.understanding among the population by providing soft skills and leadership.training, dialogue facilitation strategies to reduce grievances, and building.social cohesion as a strategy to prevent VEO recruitment. USAID Tamkeen will.help counter the devastating effects of panic, fear, and isolation resulting.from disinformation that supports the malign and divisive tactics employed by.VE actors and entities. USAID Tamkeen is also aligned with Mission Objective.2.2 from the Mauritania Integrated Country Strategy: Citizens are empowered.through policies promoting education, youth development, abolishment of slavery.and its effects, and integration of refugees, stateless persons, and.marginalized communities..</narrative>
  </description>
